  "title": "Taweez against Dystocia (Difficult Childbirth)",
  "data": "For a woman suffering from dystocia (difficult or abnormally painful childbirth), the following holy verses may be written on a parchment and tied to her right thigh. It must be untied after she gives birth:\nبِسْمِ اللّٰهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ كَاَنَّهُمْ يَوْمَ يَرَوْنَ مَا يُوْعَدُوْنَ لَمْ يَلْبَثُوْا اِلَّا سَاعَةً مِّنْ نَهَارٍ\nBISMILLAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEMI KA-ANNAHUM YAWMA YARAWNA MAA YOO'ADOONA LAM YALBATHOO ILLAA SAA'ATAM MIN NAHAAR\nIn the Name of Allah, the Beneficent, the Merciful. On the day that they shall see what they are threatened with, (it shall be) as though they had not tarried save an hour of the day. (46:35)\nكَاَنَّهُمْ يَوْمَ يَرَوْنَهَا لَمْ يَلْبَثُوْا اِلَّا عَشِيَّةً اَوْ ضُحَاهَا\nKA-ANNAHUM YAWMA YARAWNAHAA LAM YALBATHOO ILLAA A'SHIYYATAN AW DUHAAHAA\nOn the day that they see it, (it will be) as though they had not tarried but the latter part of a day or the early part of it. (79:46)\nاِذْ قَالَتِ امْرَاَتُ عِمْرَانَ رَبِّ اِنِّىْ نَذَرْتُ لَكَ مَا فِىْ بَطْنِىْ مُحَرَّرًا فَتَقَبَّلْ مِنِّىْ اِنَّكَ اَنْتَ السَّمِيْعُ الْعَلِيْمُ\nIDH QAALATIM RA'ATU I'MRAANA RABBI INNEE NADHARTU LAKA MAA FEE BATNEE MUHARRARAN FATAQABBAL MINNEE INNAKA ANTAS SAMEE'UL A'LEEM\nWhen a woman of Imran said: My Lord! surely I vow to You what is in my womb, to be devoted (to Your service); accept therefore from me, surely You are the Hearing, the Knowing. (3:35)\nIt is also reported that the following holy verses of [Surah Maryam](A23) should be recited over a woman suffering from dystocia:\nفَاَجَاۤئَهَا الْمَخَاضُ اِلٰى جِذْعِ النَّخْلَةِ قَالَتْ يَا لَيْتَنِىْ مِتُّ قَبْلَ هٰذَا وَكُنْتُ نَسْيًا مَّنْسِيًّا\nFA-AJAA'AHAL MAKHAADU ILAA JIDH'IN NAKHLATI QAALAT YAA LAYTANEE MITTU QABLA HAADHAA WA KUNTU NASYAM MANSIYYAA\nAnd the throes (of childbirth) compelled her to betake herself to the trunk of a palm tree. She said: Oh, would that I had died before this, and had been a thing quite forgotten!\nفَنَادَاهَا مِنْ تَحْتِهَا اَلَّا تَحْزَنِىْ قَدْ جَعَلَ رَبُّكِ تَحْتَكِ سَرِيًّا\nFANAADAAHAA MIN TAHTIHAA ALLAA TAHZANEE QAD JA'ALA RABBUKI TAHTAKI SARIYYAA\nThen (the child) called out to her from beneath her: Grieve not, surely your Lord has made a stream to flow beneath you;\nوَهُزِّىْ اِلَيْكِ بِجِذْعِ النَّخْلَةِ تُسَاقِطْ عَلَيْكِ رُطَبًا جَنِيًّا\nWA HUZZEE ILAYKI BIJIDH'IN NAKHLATI TUSAAQIT A'LAYKI RUTABAN JANIYYAA\nand shake towards you the trunk of the palm tree, it will drop on you fresh ripe dates. (19:23-25)\nThe reciter should then raise the voice with the following holy verse and the words that follow it:\nوَاللّٰهُ اَخْرَجَكُمْ مِنْ بُطُوْنِ اُمَّهَاتِكُمْ لَا تَعْلَمُوْنَ شَيْئًا وَجَعَلَ لَكُمُ السَّمْعَ وَالْاَبْصَارَ وَالْاَفْئِدَةَ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُوْنَ\nWALLAAHU AKHRAJAKUM MIN BUTOONI UMMAHAATIKUM LAA TA'LAMOONA SHAY'AN WA JA'ALA LAKUMUS SAM'A WAL ABSAARA WAL AF'IDATA LA'ALLAKUM TASHKUROON\nAnd Allah has brought you forth from the wombs of your mothers - you did not know anything - and He gave you hearing and sight and hearts that you may give thanks. (16:78)\nكَذٰلِكَ اُخْرُجْ اَيُّهَا الطَّلْقُ اُخْرُجْ بِاِذْنِ اللّٰهِ\nKADHAALIKA UKHRUJ AYYUHAT TALQU UKHRUJ BI-IDHNILLAAH\nIn like manner, come out, O labor! Come out by the permission of Allah.\nFor easy childbirth, Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) is reported to have advised writing the following supplicatory prayer on a sheet of paper or a parchment:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ فَارِجَ الْهَمِّ وَكَاشِفَ الْغَمِّ وَرَحْمٰنَ الدُّنْيَا وَالْاٰخِرَةِ وَرَحِيْمَهُمَا\nALLAAHUMMA FAARIJAL HAMMI WA KAASHIFAL GHAMMI WA RAHMAANAD DUNYAA WAL AAKHIRATI WA RAHEEMAHUMAA\nO Allah, Reliever of anxiety, Remover of grief, the Beneficent of this world and the Hereafter and the Merciful of both,\nاِرْحَمْ فُلَانَةَ بِنْتَ فُلَانَةَ رَحْمَةً تُغْنِيْهَا بِهَا عَنْ رَّحْمَةِ جَمِيْعِ خَلْقِكَ\nIRHAM FULAANATA BINTA FULAANATA RAHMATAN TUGHNEEHAA BIHAA A'N RAHMATI JAMEE'I KHALQIK\nhave mercy on so-and-so, the daughter of so-and-so, with a mercy by which You free her from need of the mercy of all Your creatures,\nتُفَرِّجُ بِهَا كُرْبَتَهَا وَتَكْشِفُ بِهَا غَمَّهَا وَتُيَسِّرُ بِهَا وِلَادَتَهَا\nTUFARRIJU BIHAA KURBATAHAA WA TAKSHIFU BIHAA GHAMMAHAA WA TUYASSIRU BIHAA WILAADATAHAA\nby which You relieve her distress, remove her grief and make her delivery easy.\nوَقُضِىَ بَيْنَهُمْ بِالْحَقِّ وَهُمْ لَا يُظْلَمُوْنَ وَقِيْلَ الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ\nWA QUDIYA BAYNAHUM BIL HAQQI WA HUM LAA YUZLAMOONA WA QEELAL HAMDU LILLAAHI RABBIL A'ALAMEEN\nAnd judgment shall be given between them with justice, and they shall not be dealt with unjustly, and it shall be said: All praise is due to Allah, the Lord of the worlds.\nIn place of “so-and-so, the daughter of so-and-so”, mention the woman's name and her mother's name."
